----------------------------------------------------------------------
Points to make in Chapter 4:
----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. With N=25250, statistical significance is easy to obtain. Report the
   confidence interval on the accuracy difference alongside every
   p-value, and discuss whether the gap is large enough to matter for
   dietary assessment in practice.
2. McNemar and Wilcoxon can disagree. McNemar weights every image
   equally, so frequent classes dominate; Wilcoxon weights every class
   equally. A disagreement means one model wins on common classes while
   the other wins on more classes overall, which is a finding about
   error structure and belongs in the Research Question 2 discussion.
3. State the correction explicitly. An uncorrected family of 15 tests
   at alpha=0.05 carries roughly a 54 percent chance of at least one
   false positive.

Experiment 9 complete. No GPU was used.
